      "content": "ABOUT THE MAJOR The Bachelor of Arts in Business Administration with an emphasis in Project Management is designed to provide expansive knowledge and a practical guide to leadership and management, within the field of project management. Classes such as management, organizational behavior, marketing, and accounting provide the foundation for advanced classes in project management. The key to this 24 month program is a consistent focus on participation, application of theories and concepts, and performance. With our bachelor's degree emphasis in Project Management, graduates will complete four courses designed specifically for students who want to gain knowledge in project management. Threaded throughout the major is an ethical employee and leadership perspective. The major is designed to provide a solid background for graduates to use in seeking responsible employment, promotion, or Project Management certifications (CAPM or PMP). **Agreement does not include all required courses for the major at FPU** This agreement lists courses that are prerequisites or may be completed prior to transfer to satisfy major requirements. All transfer courses must be completed with a grade of C- or better, and students must complete a minimum of 18 units in the major at FPU. Please contact an academic advisor to discuss the recommended sequence of courses, including courses that may count for both GE and major requirements. To view the full degree requirements, please refer to the Undergraduate Catalog: https://catalog.fresno.edu/index.php .",
